      "review": {
        "verdict": "bug",
        "confidence": 0.85,
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "contract-violation",
        "title": "parse_rfc3339 accepts trailing garbage after 'Z' (e.g. \"...00ZZ\")",
        "reason": "The strict `parse_rfc3339` only checks that the last byte is 'Z' or that the string ends with \"+00:00\", then hands off to `parse_rfc3339_weak`. In the weak parser, the no-fraction branch at date.rs:187 rejects the input only when `len > 25` or `b[19]` is neither 'Z' nor the full \"+00:00\". As a result, \"…00ZZ\" and \"…00Zabc+00:00\" (up to 25 bytes) pass, even though the docs say only `Z` or `+00:00` is supported for this strict function. The fix is simple (require `b.len()==20` with 'Z', or exactly `+00:00` at b[19..]), so a maintainer would likely accept it, though the impact is minor.",
        "maintainerWouldFix": true
      },
      "status": "confirmed",
      "bugId": "PH-001",
      "reproSource": "use humantime::parse_rfc3339;\n\n#[test]\nfn repro_trailing_garbage() {\n    assert!(parse_rfc3339(\"1970-01-01T00:00:00ZZ\").is_err());\n    assert!(parse_rfc3339(\"1970-01-01T00:00:00Zabc+00:00\").is_err());\n}\n",
      "bugDir": ".proofhound/runs/20261017-170259/bugs/PH-001-parse-rfc3339-accepts-trailing-garbage-after-z-e"
    },
